// fe4 per-stage PyTorch parity for the Hikoboshi-ESM2-8M soft-SW pipeline.
//
// Loads `tests/cpp/data/esm2_softsw_step_goldens.npz` (generated by
// `scripts/esm2_softsw_step_goldens.py`) and exercises the full Hikoboshi
// C++ pipeline on the same three lead-diagnostic SCOPe40-test-v2 pairs
// used by fe1/fe2. For each pair the test asserts every stage against
// the PyTorch reference with the public parity-contract tolerance:
//
//   Stage 0 (token_ids)         : bit-exact (CLS=26, residues, EOS=27)
//   Stage 1 (encoder output)    : <= 1e-4 max-abs delta per cell (fast)
//   Stage 2 (sim_matrix)        : <= 1e-4 max-abs delta per cell (fast)
//   Stage 3 (log_partition)     : <= max(abs, rel*magnitude)       (fast)
//   Stage 4 (V = match_alpha)   : <= max(abs, rel*magnitude)/cell  (fast)
//   Stage 5 (M = match_beta)    : <= 1e-4 max-abs delta per cell   (fast)
//   Stage 6 (posterior)         : <= 1e-4 max-abs delta per cell   (fast)
//   Stage 7 (path.steps)        : bit-exact coordinate set
//
// Strict mode tightens stages 1-6 to the 1e-5 public parity-contract bar;
// stages 3 and 4 apply that bar as a magnitude-relative tolerance. Honor
// strict mode through the `HIKOBOSHI_PARITY_MODE=strict` env (matches the
// existing parity tests).
//
// On any stage failure the test prints:
//   - the failing pair id
//   - the failing stage name
//   - max-abs delta + worst-cell coordinate(s)
//   - the corresponding fe5 dispatch hint (D1.stage)
// and exits 1 so `meson test --suite parity-pytorch` reports the failure.

